  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "DC load line, AC load line and Q-point"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "With no signal, $V_{CE} = V_{CC} - I_C(R_C + R_E)$. On the output characteristics this is the DC load line, joining the cut-off point $(V_{CC}, 0)$ to the saturation point $(0,\\ V_{CC}/(R_C+R_E))$. For the signal, $C_E$ shorts $R_E$ and $C_C$ connects $R_L$, so the AC load is $r_L = R_C \\parallel R_L$ and the AC load line through Q is steeper. The Q-point is placed near the middle of the load line so the output can swing equally both ways without clipping."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Cut-off point: VCE = VCC, IC = 0"
    },
    {
     "en": "Saturation point: IC = VCC/(RC + RE)"
    },
    {
     "en": "AC load rL = RC ∥ RL"
    },
    {
     "en": "Q at the centre gives the largest undistorted swing"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The DC load line joins VCC on the voltage axis to VCC over RC plus RE on the current axis. Keep the Q-point in the middle for the biggest clean output.",
    "kn": "ಡಿಸಿ ಲೋಡ್ ರೇಖೆ ವೋಲ್ಟೇಜ್ ಅಕ್ಷದ VCC ಯನ್ನು ಪ್ರವಾಹ ಅಕ್ಷದ VCC/(RC + RE) ಗೆ ಸೇರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. AC ಲೋಡ್ rL = RC ∥ RL. ವಿಕೃತಿ ಇಲ್ಲದ ಗರಿಷ್ಠ ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್‌ಗಾಗಿ ಕ್ಯೂ-ಬಿಂದುವನ್ನು ಲೋಡ್ ರೇಖೆಯ ಮಧ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಇಡುತ್ತಾರೆ."
   },
   "formula": "I_{C(sat)} = \\frac{V_{CC}}{R_C + R_E}, \\qquad r_L = \\frac{R_C R_L}{R_C + R_L}"
  },
