   "id": "ex1",
   "type": "example",
   "problem": {
    "en": "In a CE amplifier VCC = 12 V, RC = 2 kΩ, RE = 1 kΩ and IC = 2 mA at the Q-point. Find VCE and the two end points of the DC load line."
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "VCE = VCC − IC(RC + RE) = 12 − 2 mA × 3 kΩ = 12 − 6 = 6 V."
    },
    {
     "en": "Cut-off point: IC = 0, VCE = VCC = 12 V."
    },
    {
     "en": "Saturation point: VCE = 0, IC(sat) = 12 V / 3 kΩ = 4 mA."
    },
    {
     "en": "Q (6 V, 2 mA) is exactly at the middle of the load line."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "VCE = 6 V; load line from (12 V, 0) to (0, 4 mA)"
   },
   "narration": {
    "en": "Let us work this out together. In a CE amplifier VCC = 12 V, RC = 2 kΩ, RE = 1 kΩ and IC = 2 mA at the Q-point. Find VCE and the two end points of the DC load line."
   }
